      "taskType": "modeling",
      "prompt": "A device is worth ${{v0}} initially and loses {{pct}}% of its value each year. Formulate the explicit exponential value model AND an equivalent recursive model beginning at year 0.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "factor",
          "label": "Annual retained-value factor",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{factor}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "explicit",
          "label": "Explicit model $V(t)$",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "expected": "V={{v0}}({{factor}})^t"
        },
        {
          "id": "initial",
          "label": "Recursive initial condition",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "expected": "V_0={{v0}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "recursive",
          "label": "Recursive step",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "expected": "V_n={{factor}}V_(n-1)"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Percent decay uses the portion retained each period.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Losing {{pct}}% means retaining {{retainPct}}%, so the multiplier is {{factor}}.",
          "The explicit model uses that multiplier as the exponential base.",
          "The recursive model uses the same multiplier from one year to the next."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "$V={{v0}}({{factor}})^t$; $V_0={{v0}},\\;V_n={{factor}}V_{n-1}$"
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "A decay model still uses multiplication; the factor is less than 1 rather than subtracting the same dollar amount each year."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Retained percent = 100 − decay percent."
      ],
